senses.gloss:
múkha, n.
 —1. mouth, 39^3, 40^10, 51^12;
jaws, 18^23;
 —2. visage, countenance,
face, 13^3; snout or face of an animal,
44^12; at end of cpds, esp. w. an adj.
[1298a], or adjectively used prep. [1305],
or adv. [1306] denoting direction: udaṅmukha,
having a northward face, turning
northward; abhi-mukha, having the face
towards;
 —3. (like Eng. face) surface,
25^21;
 —4. (like Eng. head, and like chief
from caput) the head, i. e. chief, best,
most excellent, 51^22.
